From: Hummingbird <hummingbird@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bump hono 4.13.7 -> 4.13.11 for CVE-2026-109955

Upstream: https://github.com/honojs/hono/releases/tag/v4.13.11

Hono from 4.12.4 before 4.13.11 contains a middleware bypass
vulnerability in serveStatic: the request path is decoded once for
routing, then decoded a second time before resolving the file. A
crafted request with a malformed percent-encoded path can be routed
as one path by the router but served as another by serveStatic,
letting an unauthenticated attacker skip prefix middleware (such as
an authentication check) and reach the static file anyway. Fixed in
4.13.11 by rejecting request paths that still contain "%" after the
first decode (GHSA-5r4p-p66f-jhc7).
Yarn cache regenerated and uploaded to lookaside.

--- a/package.json
+++ b/package.json
@@ -472,7 +472,8 @@
     "js-yaml@npm:^4.2.0": "4.3.2",
     "joi@npm:^17.11.0": "17.13.8",
     "joi@npm:^18.2.1": "18.2.9",
-    "axios": "1.20.0"
+    "axios": "1.20.0",
+    "hono": "4.13.11"
   },
   "workspaces": {
     "packages": [
--- a/yarn.lock
+++ b/yarn.lock
@@ -20121,10 +20121,10 @@
